      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T09:09:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How many of these do we think we\u0027ll be keeping ?\n\nA HashMap of HashMaps seems extremely expensive, especially considering you\u0027ll almost always have at most one of these, and the keys are Network (which is a glorified integer) and Integer.\n\nLook at comments below as I\u0027m not sure you\u0027ll need this at all, but you could just add a boolean to `KeepaliveInfo` and just use the map above ? Or if you really need a different data structure, it could just be an ArrayList\u003c\u003e of a struct with Network, int and KeepaliveInfo, and perform linear search ? That will likely be much faster than a hashmap of hashmaps.",
      "range": {
