      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T09:09:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you fundamentally changing the semantics of `mStopReason` here ?\n\nKeepaliveTracker is written like a state machine with the state stored in mStartedState with the following state graph :\nNOT_STARTED 🠊 STARTING 🠊 STARTED 🠊 STOPPING 🠊 NOT_STARTED. A fair bit of code is written to handle the various transitions (e.g. the STOPPING 🠊 NOT_STARTED transition will call `unlinkDeathRecipient` because at that point there is nothing left to clean up if the caller dies). Once a keepalive is stopped, it can\u0027t be restarted and the stop reason is latched.\n\nIt seems to me like your patch is changing this by making the sum of `mStartedState+mStopReason` the new state, so you\u0027re adding a large number of states ; for example, a keepalive can now be in `STOPPING+TEMP_DISABLED` state. This is fairly confusing.\n\nI think you need to do one of two things :\n• Change the state machine in this file, and to comment very carefully what the new state machine looks like.\n• Do not change the state machine in this file, and handle the additional state elsewhere (e.g. in ConnectivityService).\n\nTo me the latter seems a little bit wiser considering your current code – since disabling temporarily seems to be using the entire start/stop machinery, including linking and unlinking the death recipient and closing the FD for example, it sounds to me like having an independent piece of state is less dangerous than having all these tests to skip part of the logic if TEMP_DISABLED.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 457,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 457,
        "endChar": 94
      },
